Amiga 1200 core: the third-party CPU of this core. Read cores/amiga/rtl/NOTICE for the terms of the rest of the Amiga
gateware. No ROM is in this repository.
Rights holders who see a problem with any part listed here: please contact us, and we remove the part concerned.

TG68K - the 68020 of the Amiga 1200 core
  Upstream   https://github.com/MiSTle-Dev/NanoMig, commit a19604a19a6100033a29281d2be3287b65bc9c0e (the commit cores/amiga/rtl/NOTICE
             names), src/tg68k/ and sim/. TG68K.C by Tobias Gubener (opencores), patches by MikeJ, Till Harbaum, Rok Krajnc and others.
  Licence    GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3 or (at your option) any later version. Read from the headers of the files
             themselves ("Copyright (c) 2009-2020 Tobias Gubener ... GNU Lesser General Public License ... either version 3 of the
             License, or (at your option) any later version", the same text in all three VHDL files). NanoMig's repository has no
             LICENSE file. (The sentence "GNU General Public License for more details" in the header is the boilerplate of the LGPL notice, not a second licence.)
  Taken      rtl/tg68k/TG68K_Pack.vhd, TG68K_ALU.vhd and TG68KdotC_Kernel.vhd, unchanged except that the kernel's entity is renamed
             TG68KdotC_Kernel -> TG68KdotC_Kernel_core (three lines, tools/vendor_tg68k.sh does it): rtl/tg68k_020.v (ours) takes
             the old name because cpu_wrapper.v instantiates it, and ties the kernel's CPU input to 11 (68020).
             sim/tg68k/TG68KdotC_Kernel.v: NanoMig's sim/TG68KdotC_Kernel.v byte for byte, the tool-generated Verilog translation
             of the same kernel that Verilator needs (no VHDL there). A derivative of the LGPL VHDL, so LGPL. Simulation only.
  Not taken  TG68K.vhd (the 68000 bus top, nothing instantiates it), src/tg68k/verilog/ (an unfinished AI translation that upstream
             says fails in the first instruction), the cache (cpu_cache_new.v).
  Linking    The LGPL case that matters: the kernel is a separate design unit with its own entity and is not modified beyond the rename,
             so a user can replace it.

rtl/cpu_wrapper.v is cores/amiga/rtl/src/minimig-aga/cpu_wrapper.v (Minimig-AGA, GPL v3 or later, see cores/amiga/rtl/NOTICE) with
one change, rtl/cpu_wrapper.diff; tools/check_wrapper_fork.sh fails when either side moves. rtl/tg68k_020.v is ours.
